From: OpenATV RetroGaming <noreply@openatv.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: do not require unrequested FFmpeg components

FindFFmpeg probes every known FFmpeg library so that imported targets can be
created when they are available.  The pkg-config fallback incorrectly marks
each probe REQUIRED, including optional and unrequested libraries such as
libpostproc.  FFmpeg 8 no longer ships libpostproc, while PPSSPP only requests
avcodec, avformat, avutil, swresample and swscale.

Keep the probe quiet and optional.  find_package_handle_standard_args already
checks the components requested by find_package(FFmpeg REQUIRED ...), so a
genuinely required component still fails configuration.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 cmake/Modules/FindFFmpeg.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/Modules/FindFFmpeg.cmake b/cmake/Modules/FindFFmpeg.cmake
index 4f038c0..899d775 100644
--- a/cmake/Modules/FindFFmpeg.cmake
+++ b/cmake/Modules/FindFFmpeg.cmake
@@ -106,6 +106,6 @@ function(find_ffmpeg LIBNAME)
     # Didn't find it in the usual paths, try pkg-config
     find_package(PkgConfig QUIET)
-    pkg_check_modules(FFmpeg_PKGCONFIG_${LIBNAME} REQUIRED QUIET lib${LIBNAME})
+    pkg_check_modules(FFmpeg_PKGCONFIG_${LIBNAME} QUIET lib${LIBNAME})
 
     find_path(FFmpeg_INCLUDE_${LIBNAME} lib${LIBNAME}/${_FFmpeg_HEADER_${LIBNAME}}.h
       ${FFmpeg_PKGCONFIG_${LIBNAME}_INCLUDE_DIRS}
